Part 1: qualification, synthetic credentials only
Q1 Fake-CLI self-test about 3 minutes.
Q2 Start a synthetic computer then Q3 Terminal self-check
Q4: open the attacker page (see the runbook) in another tab and let it finish, then come back.
Q5 Qualification report
Q6 Stop the synthetic computer then Q7 Wipe
Part 2: real accounts
Start computer A then open the terminal (open for 20 minutes; re-open).
In the terminal: claude auth login --claudeai, open the link, sign in, paste the code back. Then codex login --device-auth, open the link, sign in, enter the code. Close the terminal tab.
After sign-in: audit, checkpoints, forced refresh
Computer B: restore older workspace + newer credentials
Computer C: restore, then sign out of both
Computer D: restore; both must stay signed out
Stop and wipe everything stored then Download results

Recover: sign out and verify only if a step failed. Stop Force stop (credentials may be lost)

